P1 user-theme-dir-hook (Aether Serial Bridge, master §3.4 / WS-2; INV-52)

ThemeManager::scanAvailableThemes() asks the host for the user theme directory
(aetherUserThemeDir(), declared in ThemeManagerHost.h) and wraps the whole
user-dir block in `if (!userDir.isEmpty())`. AetherSDR's own host returns the
previous expression, GenericConfigLocation + "/AetherSDR/themes", so its
behaviour is unchanged. Aether Serial Bridge returns "": no user directory is
checked, listed or opened (an empty QDir would mean the working directory).

Carries a GPL-3.0 section 5(a) modification notice. Offered upstream (R1).
Test: tests/tst_ThemePatches.cpp (noUserDirScan, emptyHookScansNothingInCwd).

